<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  launchd job description for SentryFanDaemon — the root helper that writes
  SMC fan keys. Installed into
  Sentry.app/Contents/Library/LaunchDaemons/ and registered by
  `SMAppService.daemon(plistName:)` from `PrivilegedFanControlBackend`,
  only when the user explicitly asks for it in Settings ▸ Fans.

  THE FILE NAME IS PART OF THE API. `SMAppService.daemon(plistName:)` looks
  this file up by basename inside Contents/Library/LaunchDaemons, and
  launchd requires `Label` below to equal that basename minus ".plist".
  Both come from `FanDaemonNaming.label`, and `FanDaemonNamingTests` pins
  the exact string so renaming one without the other fails a test rather
  than producing a silently unregistrable helper.

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT

  RunAtLoad / KeepAlive
      Both omitted, which means both default to false: this daemon is
      launched *on demand*, when something connects to its Mach service,
      and it is allowed to exit. That is the opposite of what a daemon
      usually wants and exactly what this one needs — `FanDaemonFailSafe`
      exits the process after 60 seconds with no client, and `KeepAlive`
      would have launchd immediately resurrect the root process the
      fail-safe just retired. A daemon that cannot stay dead cannot be the
      mitigation for a leaked daemon.

  Sockets / StandardOutPath / StandardErrorPath / EnvironmentVariables
      A root process should read nothing it does not need. Logging goes to
      the unified log via `os.Logger`, which needs no file this daemon
      would have to create, own, and rotate as root.

  ProgramArguments
      `BundleProgram` is used instead — a path relative to the app bundle,
      which is what lets the daemon move with the app instead of hardcoding
      an absolute /Applications path that a user who keeps apps elsewhere
      would break. It also takes no arguments, because there is no argument
      it should accept.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>dev.malekswilam.macstat.fandaemon</string>

	<!-- Relative to Sentry.app. The MacStat target's Copy Files phase puts
	     the built tool at Contents/MacOS/SentryFanDaemon; see project.yml. -->
	<key>BundleProgram</key>
	<string>Contents/MacOS/SentryFanDaemon</string>

	<!-- Must match FanDaemonNaming.machService exactly — the app dials this
	     string via NSXPCConnection(machServiceName:options:.privileged). -->
	<key>MachServices</key>
	<dict>
		<key>dev.malekswilam.macstat.fandaemon</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>

	<!-- What macOS shows the user in System Settings ▸ General ▸ Login
	     Items & Extensions. Without it the entry is an unexplained
	     background item; with it, it is attributed to Sentry, which is the
	     only honest presentation of a root process this app installed. It
	     is also the entry the user toggles off to disable the helper
	     without deleting anything. -->
	<key>AssociatedBundleIdentifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>dev.malekswilam.macstat</string>
	</array>

	<!-- Adaptive: the daemon spends essentially all its time asleep on a
	     dispatch queue, but a fan write should not be scheduled behind a
	     background maintenance task. -->
	<key>ProcessType</key>
	<string>Adaptive</string>
</dict>
</plist>
